  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "White phosphorus on reaction with limited supply of oxygen gives lower oxide $P_4 \\mathrm{O}_6$. Therefore, air $\\left(\\mathrm{O}_2+\\mathrm{N}_2\\right)$ is a good source for controlled supply of oxygen and the best choice for controlled oxidation of white phosphorus into lower oxide $\\mathrm{P}_4 \\mathrm{O}_6$.",
